\subsection{General Information}
This synthesis follows standard organic chemistry protocols. Propan-2-yl methylphosphonofluoridate (PMPF) is prepared via the phosphoramidite reaction of 2-methyl-1,2,5-triazol-1-yl-4,6,7,8-tetraacetic acid with Pd(PPh₃)₄. The key steps involve the preparation of the phosphoramidite core, the phosphoramide coupling reagents, and the treatment of the resulting product with NaOH or HCl. Due to the high reactivity of phosphoramidites, the synthesis requires strict temperature control and protective equipment.

\subsection{General Instructions}
The following steps are recommended for a typical laboratory setup:
1. Prepare a 1000 mL solution of sodium hydroxide (NaOH) in methanol.
2. Add 2 equivalents of 2-methyl-1,2,5-triazol-1-yl-4,6,7,8-tetraacetic acid (50 mL) to the NaOH solution.
3. Continue adding 2 equivalents of phosphoric acid (10 mL) at room temperature.
4. Final step: NaOH was added twice, phosphoric acid was added twice, and the mixture was stirred for an additional 10 minutes at room temperature.

Always wear gloves and goggles when handling strong acids and alkaline reagents.

